# Dirty Pipe-Style Race Condition Exploit

## Overview

This exploit targets a race condition similar to CVE-2022-0847 (Dirty Pipe), where an unprivileged user can overwrite data in arbitrary readable files, even those they don't own. The key insight is exploiting a window where the kernel's page cache and file permission checks are inconsistent.

## The Vulnerability Concept

Dirty Pipe worked because `pipe_buffer` flags weren't initialized on splice, allowing `PIPE_BUF_FLAG_CAN_MERGE` to persist across splice operations. Our variant exploits a **race window** between permission checking and the actual write to the page cache.

