## Overview

This uses the classic **CommonsCollections6** gadget chain (works on commons-collections 3.x without requiring JRE version constraints like CC1/CC3):

```
ObjectInputStream.readObject()
  → AnnotationInvocationHandler.readObject()      [CC 3.1–3.2.1]
  → ...
```

Actually, **CC6** avoids `AnnotationInvocationHandler` entirely (which was restricted in newer JDKs), making it the most portable choice:

```
java.io.ObjectInputStream.readObject()
  → org.apache.commons.collections.keyvalue.TiedMapEntry.hashCode()
    → LazyMap.get()
      → ChainedTransformer.transform()
        → ConstantTransformer → InvokerTransformer → InvokerTransformer → InvokerTransformer
          → Runtime.getRuntime().exec("...")
```

